'''Chimaera & Manticore Campaigns'''

Both versions share the same 13‑Gym League, but differ in encounter tables, version exclusives, and late‑game narrative details.

= Gym League Overview =

The League is distributed across '''six major cities''', each hosting '''two Gyms''', plus a final Heroic Gym located in a dedicated end‑game area.  
This structure reduces mapping workload while keeping progression clear and consistent across both campaigns.

Collecting all '''13 Badges''' grants access to the '''Champion’s Tournament''', replacing the traditional Elite Four.

= City Structure =

Below are the cities used in both campaigns, with short etymology notes and flavour descriptions.

* '''Hearthrock City''' — Normal & Earth  
: *Etymology:* “Hearth” for warmth, “rock” for stability.  

* '''Steamshore City''' — Water & Fire  
: *Etymology:* “Steam” from heat, “shore” from the coast.  

* '''Thornwood City''' — Wood & Venom  
: *Etymology:* “Thorn” for sharp growth, “wood” for the forest.  

* '''Stormpeak City''' — Frost & Lightning  
: *Etymology:* “Storm” for rough weather, “peak” for height.  

* '''Aerolume City''' — Metal & Sky  
: *Etymology:* “Aero” for air, “lume” for shine.  

* '''Umbrastar City''' — Shadow & Cosmic  
: *Etymology:* “Umbra” for shade, “star” for the night sky.  

* '''Valorhold City''' — Heroic (Final Area)  
: *Etymology:* “Valor” for courage, “hold” for a strong place.  

= Map Progression =

Below is the full travel order used in both campaigns, listing each city and the route that follows it.  
All maps use the naming format: ''mods/tuxemon/maps/classic_<name>.tmx''

== City and Route Layout ==

=== Main path (Hearthrock → Umbrastar) ===
* '''Hearthrock City''' → ''mods/tuxemon/maps/classic_hearthrock_city.tmx''
* '''Route 1''' → ''mods/tuxemon/maps/classic_route_1.tmx''
* '''Steamshore City''' → ''mods/tuxemon/maps/classic_steamshore_city.tmx''
